  "article_paraphrase": "She is known for her ability to see beyond the ordinary and is the daughter of one of Europe's most enduring monarchs; he identifies as a shaman with Californian roots going back six generations. Princess Märtha Louise of Norway’s marriage to Durek Verrett on Saturday was far from a typical royal celebration, but that didn’t deter onlookers who crowded the grey, cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to spot the bride. The only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, 52-year-old Märtha Louise is currently fourth in the succession for the Norwegian crown. Her wedding to 49-year-old Verrett, held in a Norwegian church ceremony, was celebrated at the Hotel Union in Geiranger, a small village situated below picturesque fjords, with both royals and celebrities among the attendees. Märtha Louise was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to the late Norwegian writer Ari Behn, whom she divorced in 2017. The guest list, numbering 350, featured her brother Crown Prince Haakon and his wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit; Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel; as well as Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Märtha Louise’s royal life has been anything but traditional—she has publicly stated she is clairvoyant and ran a healing school for a decade, where she guided people in connecting with angels. In 2022, she announced her decision to withdraw from her formal royal duties to concentrate on her joint ventures with Verrett and to set clearer boundaries between their work and Norway’s royal family. Verrett calls himself an 'energy activator' and a 'servant of God' on Instagram, with a celebrity clientele that includes Goop founder Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he refers to as a 'soul sister.'"
}
